        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "85f98759-7e0f-565c-8484-bc7f7eec1e48",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fannie Lee Chaney, James Earl Chaney\n- Organizations: Ku Klux Klan\n- Places: Meridian, Mississippi; Philadelphia, Mississippi; Mississippi\n- Events: Freedom Summer, 1964 murders of civil rights workers\n- Roles: Baker, civil rights activist, civil rights worker\n\nFacts:\n- James Earl Chaney was born on May 30, 1943, and he was from Meridian, Mississippi.\n- On June 21, 1964, James Earl Chaney was one of three American civil rights workers murdered by members of the Ku Klux Klan near Philadelphia, Mississippi, during Freedom Summer.\n- Fannie Lee Chaney was born on September 4, 1921.\n- Fannie Lee Chaney became a civil rights activist after her son James Chaney was murdered by the Ku Klux Klan during the 1964 Freedom Summer rides in Mississippi.\n- Fannie Lee Chaney had worked as an American baker before becoming a civil rights activist.\n- Fannie Lee Chaney died on May 22, 2007.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
